WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:10.400
Pollsters have been tracking America's reactions&nbsp;
to COVID since the pandemic began in March, 2020,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:15.680
and we have covered their findings each month&nbsp;
in the AEI Polling Report. Axios/Ipsos recently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:22.160
released their 59th weekly wave of results.&nbsp;
While concern has increased since the summer, 72%&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:27.040
in their December, 2021, poll said they plan to&nbsp;
see family or friends outside their households&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:32.080
during the winter holidays. 31% of those who&nbsp;
would see family or friends said that they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:37.360
would see people who were unvaccinated. Despite&nbsp;
the emergence of the omicron variant, pollsters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:42.000
note that few have increased the rate in which&nbsp;
they wear masks or social distance in public.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:47.360
Fifty-four percent of employed people supported&nbsp;
their employer requiring all employees to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:52.400
vaccinated — forty-five percent were opposed — and&nbsp;
a third said that their employer had implemented&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:58.560
a vaccine mandate in recent weeks. In another&nbsp;
question, 51% supported making it illegal for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:04.560
companies to deny service or employment to the&nbsp;
non-vaccinated, including 55% of Republicans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:11.120
and 46% of Democrats. How concerned are you about&nbsp;
the omicron variant? Let us know in our poll.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:15.600
Also, let us know what other topics you'd&nbsp;
like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:19.920
and be sure to like and subscribe for&nbsp;
more research and videos from AEI.

